{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism","id":1498313,"title":"I am officially confused by The Ministry schism.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-29T09:22:30-08:00","id":1498313,"title":"I am officially confused by The Ministry schism.","content":"OK, so my initial grasp of the Ministry was that there was a new schism born of a heresy that claimed there was no need to resurrect Set. Because he exists within the blood of his descendants and the belief of his worshipers who carry out his goals and aims and etc, etc. And yeah, I can see how this would cause a big row. &quot;Refusing to aid in Set's resurrection,&quot; biggest sin of the Path of Typhon. <i>Heresy. </i>Etc. (Plus a touch of rebranding to appeal to the fledglings.)<br /> <br /> Then it was that because the Ministry wanted to be polytheists instead of practicing the Setite religion of their clan(?)<br /> <br /> And now I've been told that it was because, after the final deaths of the most powerful members of the clan, Egypt no longer holds so much sway over the clan on a global scale and the Clan of Faith is 100% decentralized and all the branch cults who worship the Dark God under other masks than Set have redecorated to make him seem more cosmopolitan and less Egypt-centric to appeal to a wider net of potential converts. That... makes sense, I guess...?<br /> <br /> I have absolutely no idea what is going on over there, can anyone explain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 11-29-2022, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T11:21:59-08:00","id":1498323,"title":"","content":"The answers you seek are in <b>Beckett's Jyhad Diary</b> and <b>Cults of the Blood Gods</b><br /> <br /> There's apparently been some behind the scenes fiddling with the concept of the Setites with several people forwarding different ideas about what exactly the &quot;rebranding&quot; entails or is motivated by. Ultimately, Onyx Path Publishing's interpretation won out and they're the people who have put the most pen to paper about what the Duat is going on.<br /> <br /> The very short TLDR version is:<br /> <br /> 1. (BJD) The various Set cults have made a lot of variation on the concept of their god: Loki, Damballa (who is not evil), The World Serpent, Satanism, Eric the Goddess of Chaos, and so on. Theoretically, this is all meant to be Set in various guises but there's a lot of people who take their version of the religion more seriously than the orthodox Egyptian one.<br /> <br /> 2. (BJD) The Fire Court and Children of Wepawaut have started to work to suppress the local religious interpretations of their faith via violence. Why? <u>Because they're vampires</u>. No way was there ever not going to be a way that religion doesn't end in suppression if it means that there's a chance for more power/prestige via bloodshed.<br /> <br /> 3. (V5, Cults of the Blood Gods) This backfires <i>horribly</i>. The Ministry rebrands itself the &quot;Clan of Faith&quot; and quite a lot of members of the Followers of Set flat out drop Set completely. There's some orthodox Setites among them like Marcel and Hesha but the Ministry is now a lot more varied cult-wise. The remaining orthodox Typhonists rebrand themselves the Church of Set and it's all Set all the time.<br /> <br /> 4. It's seemingly a roughly 50-50 split in COTBG but the Ministry is more likely to be encountered than the Followers of Set because they've joined the rest of Kindred society in general and the Anarchs in particular.<br /> <br /> 5. The two sides fucking hate each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-29-2022, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T11:25:59-08:00","id":1498325,"title":"","content":"Random Aside: Basically, OPP has a job of making V5 lore make sense and it seems like every one of their books is doing emergency surgery to save the lore.<br /> <br /> Seriously, V5's appeal to me is mostly from their work.<br /> <br /> Every book is the best of the V5 line.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T11:50:30-08:00","id":1498328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498325#post1498325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random Aside: Basically, OPP has a job of making V5 lore make sense and it seems like every one of their books is doing emergency surgery to save the lore.<br /> <br /> Seriously, V5's appeal to me is mostly from their work.<br /> <br /> Every book is the best of the V5 line.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#4D5156\">I get you are trying to make inroads into V5 not-supporters by underlining more and more the role of OPP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, but we shouldn't forget that OPP was put in charge of making books for V5 not because the Evil Team of Incompetent Writers was to be stopped, but because the plan was that OPP and eventually other people would write everything besides from the Core and the two Style Guides' books ( Anarch, Camarilla).<br /> <br /> BTW, a good number of OPP freelancers worked on V5 Core, and OPP's earlier works are widely referenced in the three main manuals, starting from Beckett's Jyhad diary but going back to the other V20 books.<br /> <br /> Things have changed now with Justin and Renegade, but as far as we know it's not like &quot;<i>OPP came in as the White Knight and saved the franchise</i>&quot;: OPP did the job they were tasked and, as with most of their content, they did it well.<br /> <br /> Coming back to the OP, <span style=\"color:#4D5156\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">CTPhipps has basically naile</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#4D5156\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">d </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#4D5156\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">down the facts: </span></span></span>I wish <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> had greater information on the Ministry: the bit on the Church of Set was necessary, but it was mostly an extrapolation of earlier Setite lore. A greater focus on the Ministry and their new many dresses would have been interesting.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T13:11:53-08:00","id":1498340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498328#post1498328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#202124][FONT=arial][SIZE=14px][COLOR=#4D5156]I get you are trying to make inroads into V5 not-supporters by underlining more and more the role of OPP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, but we shouldn't forget that OPP was put in charge of making books for V5 not because the Evil Team of Incompetent Writers was to be stopped, but because the plan was that OPP and eventually other people would write everything besides from the Core and the two Style Guides' books ( Anarch, Camarilla).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except I believe it was actually, &quot;They made a pitch for the books, Paradox accepted allowing them to do them, and they raised the money via Kickstarter.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is the same for any 3rd party contractor.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T13:15:57-08:00","id":1498342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498340#post1498340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except I believe it was actually, &quot;They made a pitch for the books, Paradox accepted allowing them to do them, and they raised the money via Kickstarter.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is the same for any 3rd party contractor.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At the time, if I'm not mistaken, it was NuWW accepting pitches: I think it's fairly unrealistic to think that OPP basically carved its own V5 kingdom surpassing NuWW, outside the boundaries of a general editorial strategy.<br /> <br /> Also OPP kickstarted books weren't just &quot;3rd party books&quot;, they were the backbone of the V5 line for a couple of years. It's not a situation like d20 products, where you can apply the license and do what you want without particular oversight from the brand developers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 11-29-2022, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T14:02:53-08:00","id":1498346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498342#post1498342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the time, if I'm not mistaken, it was NuWW accepting pitches: I think it's fairly unrealistic to think that OPP basically carved its own V5 kingdom surpassing NuWW, outside the boundaries of a general editorial strategy.<br /> <br /> Also OPP kickstarted books weren't just &quot;3rd party books&quot;, they were the backbone of the V5 line for a couple of years. It's not a situation like d20 products, where you can apply the license and do what you want without particular oversight from the brand developers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether you do or don't, I think it was fundamentally informed by the culture and desires of OPP's staff and experience with the setting.<br /> <br /> But that's just my opinion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T14:05:01-08:00","id":1498348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498346#post1498346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whether you do or don't, I think it was fundamentally informed by the culture and desires of OPP's staff and experience with the setting.<br /> <br /> But that's just my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's for sure, but I think it doesn't mean it's incompatible or a stand alone parallel to the rest of the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T14:06:19-08:00","id":1498349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498348#post1498348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's for sure, but I think it doesn't mean it's incompatible or a stand alone parallel to the rest of the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think its a fantastic interpretation of the line that significantly improves on the portrayal in other books.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T14:19:07-08:00","id":1498352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498349#post1498349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I think its a fantastic interpretation of the line that significantly improves on the portrayal in other books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do agree, I just think it's better not to risk building any other artificial walls between segments of the fandom: there's enough bad blood between V20 and V5 fans, better not create additional barriers between OPP V5 Fans, Martin V5 fans, Justin V5 fans and maybe the lonely Modiphius Fall of London V5 fans (I'm a bit sad they didn't give us the promised miniatures).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T16:12:39-08:00","id":1498376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498325#post1498325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random Aside: Basically, OPP has a job of making V5 lore make sense and it seems like every one of their books is doing emergency surgery to save the lore.<br /> <br /> Seriously, V5's appeal to me is mostly from their work.<br /> <br /> Every book is the best of the V5 line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to note that on the Ministry/Followers split, this was something that was was hinted as coming in V20 material, specifically Tome of Secrets, which spent time focusing more on the divisions of the Followers and essentially said, &quot;in the future there's going to be a big split.&quot; It seems likely that by 2016 when Tome of Secrets was published, the authors had some idea of the direction V5 was going and already started laying the groundwork for pieces of lore, like the Ministry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-29-2022, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T23:21:20-08:00","id":1498404,"title":"","content":"I took it as more of a pr stunt. The setites are lying through their fangs. Then again I found the ministry bland so maybe I'm bias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T02:06:14-08:00","id":1498415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498376#post1498376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to note that on the Ministry/Followers split, this was something that was was hinted as coming in V20 material, specifically Tome of Secrets, which spent time focusing more on the divisions of the Followers and essentially said, &quot;in the future there's going to be a big split.&quot; It seems likely that by 2016 when Tome of Secrets was published, the authors had some idea of the direction V5 was going and already started laying the groundwork for pieces of lore, like the Ministry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given I wrote and / or developed the Ministry / Setites in Tome of Secrets, their sections in BJD, then Anarch, then profiled a few of them in Chicago by Night, and then gave the Church of Set coverage in Cults of the Blood Gods, you would be mostly correct. These weren't laid down by Paradox or White Wolf though, but were written or developed by myself and subsequently approved. <br /> <br /> The same applies for the Hecata. The idea for the Family Reunion wasn't proposed or directed by Paradox. I laid the foundations down in Lore of the Bloodlines, Dark Ages Companion, and Tome of Secrets, developed and wrote it in greater detail in BJD, and concluded it in Cults of the Blood Gods and Trails of Ash and Bone.<br /> <br /> It may be different now, and it could be that Paradox gives firm direction to authors and developers before they start working on a book, but when I was creating content (all the way up to the official Boston by Night book you can download <a href=\"https://store.epicgames.com/en-US/p/vampire-the-masquerade-swansong--artbook\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and the material I wrote for <a href=\"https://www.vampirethemasquerade-chapters.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Chapters</a>, <a href=\"https://www.vtm-heritage.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Heritage</a>, <a href=\"https://www.everythingepic.us/vampire-the-masqurade-blood-feud\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Feud</a>, and so on) myself and the other creatives on these games would write our ideas up and then have them approved, rejected, or have amendments suggested by Paradox after those ideas were submitted, often in the form of a complete manuscript.<br /> <br /> Is that the best way to work? It depends on whether you think one's work should be governed by a firm direction at the start and work within parameters, or whether it's better to give the creative free rein and then risk rejecting the whole thing. Or maybe it should be something in between. <br /> <br /> Whatever your opinion, I was very fortunate to see so many of the ideas I came up with develop throughout V20 and into V5, some handled completely by myself, others taken on and handled by others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T02:24:43-08:00","id":1498417,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I always appreciate clarity on these subjects from designers the internal logic of setting developments and the design process fascinates me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T02:37:57-08:00","id":1498418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498415#post1498415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same applies for the Hecata. The idea for the Family Reunion wasn't proposed or directed by Paradox. I laid the foundations down in Lore of the Bloodlines, Dark Ages Companion, and Tome of Secrets, developed and wrote it in greater detail in BJD, and concluded it in Cults of the Blood Gods and Trails of Ash and Bone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Off topic from my original question, but may I ask what happened to the della Passaglia? Something happened in BJD that wasn't expanded on that I recall, and they don't have a loresheet in V5 and I don't know what would've happened to some of my characters from that family in the canon timeline. I heard a theory that the Wan Gui killed them/drove them out, but I haven't seen confirmation on that and considering the Hungry Dead apparently don't exist anymore as far as I know...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T03:16:00-08:00","id":1498419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498415#post1498415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Given I wrote and / or developed the Ministry / Setites in Tome of Secrets, their sections in BJD, then Anarch, then profiled a few of them in Chicago by Night, and then gave the Church of Set coverage in Cults of the Blood Gods, you would be mostly correct. These weren't laid down by Paradox or White Wolf though, but were written or developed by myself and subsequently approved.<br /> <br /> The same applies for the Hecata. The idea for the Family Reunion wasn't proposed or directed by Paradox. I laid the foundations down in Lore of the Bloodlines, Dark Ages Companion, and Tome of Secrets, developed and wrote it in greater detail in BJD, and concluded it in Cults of the Blood Gods and Trails of Ash and Bone.<br /> <br /> It may be different now, and it could be that Paradox gives firm direction to authors and developers before they start working on a book, but when I was creating content (all the way up to the official Boston by Night book you can download <a href=\"https://store.epicgames.com/en-US/p/vampire-the-masquerade-swansong--artbook\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and the material I wrote for <a href=\"https://www.vampirethemasquerade-chapters.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Chapters</a>, <a href=\"https://www.vtm-heritage.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Heritage</a>, <a href=\"https://www.everythingepic.us/vampire-the-masqurade-blood-feud\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Feud</a>, and so on) myself and the other creatives on these games would write our ideas up and then have them approved, rejected, or have amendments suggested by Paradox after those ideas were submitted, often in the form of a complete manuscript.<br /> <br /> Is that the best way to work? It depends on whether you think one's work should be governed by a firm direction at the start and work within parameters, or whether it's better to give the creative free rein and then risk rejecting the whole thing. Or maybe it should be something in between.<br /> <br /> Whatever your opinion, I was very fortunate to see so many of the ideas I came up with develop throughout V20 and into V5, some handled completely by myself, others taken on and handled by others.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you Matthew, your insight into creative processes is always amazing, and your work superb: as a digression, I really loved the new Boston by Night, you managed to make a very messy setting into something coeherent and interesting to play in!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T03:17:55-08:00","id":1498420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498415#post1498415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Given I wrote and / or developed the Ministry / Setites in Tome of Secrets, their sections in BJD, then Anarch, then profiled a few of them in Chicago by Night, and then gave the Church of Set coverage in Cults of the Blood Gods, you would be mostly correct. These weren't laid down by Paradox or White Wolf though, but were written or developed by myself and subsequently approved.<br /> <br /> The same applies for the Hecata. The idea for the Family Reunion wasn't proposed or directed by Paradox. I laid the foundations down in Lore of the Bloodlines, Dark Ages Companion, and Tome of Secrets, developed and wrote it in greater detail in BJD, and concluded it in Cults of the Blood Gods and Trails of Ash and Bone.<br /> <br /> It may be different now, and it could be that Paradox gives firm direction to authors and developers before they start working on a book, but when I was creating content (all the way up to the official Boston by Night book you can download <a href=\"https://store.epicgames.com/en-US/p/vampire-the-masquerade-swansong--artbook\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and the material I wrote for <a href=\"https://www.vampirethemasquerade-chapters.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Chapters</a>, <a href=\"https://www.vtm-heritage.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Heritage</a>, <a href=\"https://www.everythingepic.us/vampire-the-masqurade-blood-feud\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Feud</a>, and so on) myself and the other creatives on these games would write our ideas up and then have them approved, rejected, or have amendments suggested by Paradox after those ideas were submitted, often in the form of a complete manuscript.<br /> <br /> Is that the best way to work? It depends on whether you think one's work should be governed by a firm direction at the start and work within parameters, or whether it's better to give the creative free rein and then risk rejecting the whole thing. Or maybe it should be something in between.<br /> <br /> Whatever your opinion, I was very fortunate to see so many of the ideas I came up with develop throughout V20 and into V5, some handled completely by myself, others taken on and handled by others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification, TGG! This really is your baby.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T03:49:04-08:00","id":1498422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498418#post1498418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Off topic from my original question, but may I ask what happened to the della Passaglia? Something happened in BJD that wasn't expanded on that I recall, and they don't have a loresheet in V5 and I don't know what would've happened to some of my characters from that family in the canon timeline. I heard a theory that the Wan Gui killed them/drove them out, but I haven't seen confirmation on that and considering the Hungry Dead apparently don't exist anymore as far as I know...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We just didn't have room to cover every minor Giovanni family, so from memory their grim fate is alluded to and then quickly moved past in Beckett's Jyhad Diary, but hasn't been picked up again in V5. If there were eventually clanbooks for this edition (doubtful, but who knows), I'm sure a Clanbook: Hecata would give them, the St. Johns, Li Wengs, and all the rest some more love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T03:50:33-08:00","id":1498423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498419#post1498419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thank you Matthew, your insight into creative processes is always amazing, and your work superb: as a digression, I really loved the new Boston by Night, you managed to make a very messy setting into something coeherent and interesting to play in!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you! On the subject of books that get approved / rejected after being written, Boston by Night was originally a lot larger, but had to be cut down by about 50% to focus almost entirely on Swansong-related material. Sadly the remaining material will never be published, but I'm happy with what I wrote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T03:53:42-08:00","id":1498424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498420#post1498420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the clarification, TGG! This really is your baby.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Certain elements were maybe my foster children, but I think the important thing to remember for any creative tied to a licensed property is that it's only yours for a short tenure, and you have no control over what ultimately happens to it. Someone on one of the WoD Discords referred to my tenure as the Dawkins Era, which if put into a context of Rein\u2022Hagen era, Greenberg era, Achilli era, Webb era, etc., hopefully means it'll be remembered fondly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T04:30:05-08:00","id":1498427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498424#post1498424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certain elements were maybe my foster children, but I think the important thing to remember for any creative tied to a licensed property is that it's only yours for a short tenure, and you have no control over what ultimately happens to it. Someone on one of the WoD Discords referred to my tenure as the Dawkins Era, which if put into a context of Rein\u2022Hagen era, Greenberg era, Achilli era, Webb era, etc., hopefully means it'll be remembered fondly.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll always be remembered for<i> The Rusted Jungle</i>!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At least by me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T07:02:22-08:00","id":1498435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498313-i-am-officially-confused-by-the-ministry-schism?p=1498415#post1498415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Given I wrote and / or developed the Ministry / Setites in Tome of Secrets, their sections in BJD, then Anarch, then profiled a few of them in Chicago by Night, and then gave the Church of Set coverage in Cults of the Blood Gods, you would be mostly correct. These weren't laid down by Paradox or White Wolf though, but were written or developed by myself and subsequently approved.<br /> <br /> The same applies for the Hecata. The idea for the Family Reunion wasn't proposed or directed by Paradox. I laid the foundations down in Lore of the Bloodlines, Dark Ages Companion, and Tome of Secrets, developed and wrote it in greater detail in BJD, and concluded it in Cults of the Blood Gods and Trails of Ash and Bone.<br /> <br /> It may be different now, and it could be that Paradox gives firm direction to authors and developers before they start working on a book, but when I was creating content (all the way up to the official Boston by Night book you can download <a href=\"https://store.epicgames.com/en-US/p/vampire-the-masquerade-swansong--artbook\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and the material I wrote for <a href=\"https://www.vampirethemasquerade-chapters.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Chapters</a>, <a href=\"https://www.vtm-heritage.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Heritage</a>, <a href=\"https://www.everythingepic.us/vampire-the-masqurade-blood-feud\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Feud</a>, and so on) myself and the other creatives on these games would write our ideas up and then have them approved, rejected, or have amendments suggested by Paradox after those ideas were submitted, often in the form of a complete manuscript.<br /> <br /> Is that the best way to work? It depends on whether you think one's work should be governed by a firm direction at the start and work within parameters, or whether it's better to give the creative free rein and then risk rejecting the whole thing. Or maybe it should be something in between.<br /> <br /> Whatever your opinion, I was very fortunate to see so many of the ideas I came up with develop throughout V20 and into V5, some handled completely by myself, others taken on and handled by others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat! Thank you for that! <br /> <br /> I'm not a huge fan a lot of the stuff we've seen in 5th edition, but I did really like what happened with the Ministry and Hecata, primarily because there had been setup to that in the V20 books so it didn't feel like something that came out of left field. Neat to know that was all you, producing some of my favorite V20 vampire material and V5 material as well. Awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}